will the birds survive ozark will the  cartel or the fbi catch up with marty  first or will ruth kill just about  everyone what you need to know about  ozarks season 4 part 2 straight ahead  season 4 is the first season of ozark to  be split into two parts but fans fearing  an extended halftime hiatus needn't  worry too much instead of making us wait  for the back half of the final ozark  season netflix is gearing up to drop the  second set of episodes on april 29th a  mere three months after part 1 aired  ozark premiered its first season in july  2017 and returned for its sophomore  season in august of the next year the  third season arrived on march 27 2020.  considering ozark wrapped production on  season 4 back in october 2020 it was  always a possibility that we'd see an  accelerated release schedule but nobody  thought we'd be watching the end of  marty bird's journey as early as april  2022 netflix definitely deserves a big  pat on the back for this one  the second half of ozark season 4 is  expected to feature all of the regular  cast members from the first half with  the obvious exception of those who did  not make it out of the first seven  episodes alive all four members of the  bird family are expected to return  including marty played by jason bateman  wendy played by laura linney and the  couple's children charlotte and jonah  season four's seventh episode sanctified  saw the untimely deaths of wyatt  langmore and darlene snelangmore this  sadly leaves ruth langmore as one of the  last members of her clan left standing  julia garner has won praise for her  portrayal of ruth earning two  consecutive primetime emmy awards for  outstanding supporting actress in a  drama series we also think it's safe to  say that wyatt's younger brother three  will make an appearance at some point in  the final seven episodes it's unclear if  omar navarro or special agent maya  miller will reappear especially as  navarro was arrested by miller in the  mid-season finale  don't forget about me  but even if they don't return plenty of  emissaries of the fbi and the navarro  cartel remain additional characters we  expect to see back in the final seven  episodes of the series include javi  elizondro private investigator mel  saddam jim rattlesdorf and hannah clay  we also wouldn't be shocked to see  richard thomas return once more as  wendy's father nathan davis  the final seven episodes of ozark have a  lot hanging on the line for the bird  family while the fbi's deal with javi  would seem to be working for them at the  moment a closer inspection would  probably reveal that the deal is only  hanging on by a thread  and i really want to kill you you know  ruth has never been more distant from  marty than she is after javi murders  wyatt in the mid-season finale after she  finds wyatt and darlene's bodies ruth  holds marty at gunpoint and demands that  he tells her who killed them marty and  wendy refused to tell her but jonah  quickly outs his parents boss as a  murderer his name is javi alessandro  in the final scene of the episode ruth  promises to kill javi and screams  if you want to stop me you're gonna have  to  kill me  while ruth marty and wendy have tussled  in the past this seems like a definitive  breaking point for the two wendy and  marty are also going to have to deal  with jonah's continued rebelliousness  the young money launderer has previously  shown that he's more loyal to ruth than  his own parents something that seems to  bother wendy even more than marty we  also expect plenty of political  machinations by wendy along with the  family lawyer jim rattlesdorf since the  beginning of season 4 wendy has led the  bird foundation as a means of growing  the family's wealth power and influence  at some point ozark will also have to  catch up to the season 4 opening scene  which shows a disastrous car crash  involving all four members of the bird  family do you really think they're all  going to make it out alive  mel saddam played by adam rothenberg is  relentless yet he somehow manages to  stay calm cool and collected in the  process the former cop turned private  investigator will stop at nothing to  track down helen pierce as he was hired  by her estranged husband to discover her  whereabouts as a refresher helen was the  navarro cartel's attorney when omar  decided to have her killed allowing the  bird family to live all the same mel  continuously talks to anyone who will  hear him out as he presumably just needs  to know where helen is alive or dead  perhaps most intriguing of all is the  fact that mel has been talking to the  fbi though it would be ideal to see the  bird family make it out alive they have  dug themselves some pretty big holes  throughout ozark and it's seemingly only  a matter of time before they get caught  for one of their many crimes still fans  will have to wait and see if mel gets  his signature or whether he might play a  role in sinking the bird family  ruth is for better or worse on a rampage  she's lost virtually all of her family  members and wyatt's death is her  breaking point after all she threatens  the birds with a gun and viewers last  see her on the verge of seeking revenge  though javi is vicious ill-tempered and  seemingly thinks he's untouchable  audience members have come to discover  that you don't mess with ruth langmore  and a showdown between the two would be  pretty sweet assuming ruth comes out on  top if she did however actually pull off  her revenge chaos and madness would  likely ensue first and foremost killing  the head of the cartel is typically  frowned upon secondly the bird family  has a deal with the fbi which could be  jeopardized if hobby was to go down at  that point would the fbi have any reason  not to take marty and wendy down too  ruth may have been a trusted ally at one  point but marty and wendy likely don't  want their deal to collapse despite javi  being arguably the most savage enemy of  the bird family to date only time will  tell if ruth gets her revenge  this family's tensions aren't due to  everyday elements wendy and jonah aren't  at odds because wendy won't let jonah  say extend his curfew life-altering  mistakes have been made trust has been  destroyed and people have died i think  you have stockholm syndrome jonah has  rightfully been rebellious in season  four and he wants nothing to do with his  mother to boot since he believes she had  his uncle killed wendy didn't make  matters any better when she tried to  have jonah arrested but marty luckily  was able to put out that familial fire  surely jonah giving up javi's name to  ruth won't sit well with the family  although charlotte seems to be all in on  the family business this has only  further pushed jonah away wendy might be  more concerned with her political  ambitions right now but her family has  seemingly witnessed irreparable damage  one thing is for sure and that's that no  one is safe the car crash at the  beginning of season 4 looked fatal it's  largely speculation right now but it  would be a shame if the birds finally  reunited just for one of them to be  taken out by that crash  in a 2022 interview laura lenny was  asked if her character wendy still loved  marty and if she thought her family  would survive she told elle  yes she does love marty she does love  marty i think their relationship goes  through many different incarnations and  they are bound to each other and they're  sort of all they have they just have  each other really and i think wendy  feels that way lenny also revealed that  she relates to wendy in many ways  telling elle very much like wendy i  believe in that family as messed up as  they are as an actress i root for the  family as an actress i root for that  marriage whether it survives or not  whether the family stays together or not  i root for them though lenny's words  don't guarantee marty and wendy will  make it out alive we too are rooting for  the berg family  charlotte bird is apparently all in on  her family's business she's even  reconsidering going to college after all  why should she go when her family  already has a spot for her in their  company nonetheless we're all wondering  how her change of mind will play into  the final seven episodes of the series  though actress sophia who blitz who  plays charlotte doesn't give too much  away she has said something utterly  intriguing regarding the bird family's  ending in a 2022 interview with elle she  revealed it's a different experience for  me because it is my first major role  when we wrapped we wrapped our final  scene together as a family i won't say  what it was obviously the scene that we  filmed together was a scene as a family  that was my last scene it was wendy's  last scene it's still largely  speculative but the fact that the actors  filmed their final scene together could  mean that they were all still alive in  the end  it's not entirely marty's fault that his  family is working for the cartel but one  way or another he got them into this  mess for four seasons he has been trying  to make what he believes are the best  decisions to keep his family alive  needless to say it's been a rip-roaring  rollercoaster and we all want to know if  the series can stick the landing bateman  said in a 2020 indy wire interview  i do know where everything is going to  end i was interested in the big question  show runner chris mundy has the  opportunity to answer are they going to  get away with it or are they going to  pay a bill what does he want to message  to the audience about the consequences  of what the birds have done or lack  thereof viewers have similar questions  as it seems unlikely that this family  will receive a happily ever after  bateman also revealed we had some great  conversations about that and he's got  really good ideas about that  specifically what kind of happens at the  end of the last episode i know and it's  great if bateman believes the ending is  great then we'll take his word for it  the countdown to the end is on  in a 2022 interview with the hollywood  reporter showrunner chris mundy teased  what's to come in the final batch of  episodes explaining  i always want closure i don't want to  feel messed with i want to feel like  okay that was the end so hopefully  people will feel closure by the end  whether they like it or not i don't know  mundi also opened up about the show's  central relationship saying in terms of  tone we're going deeper into the family  and their bonds is family the ultimate  bond is friendship is marriage at what  point is it almost unhealthy to stay  even if you love somebody we're going to  delve into that with marty and wendy  hopefully the back half will still be  fun and exciting but also really  emotional for the birds and ruth  thankfully netflix has already released  a teaser trailer for ozark season 4 part  2 which mostly features a distressed  ruth on the verge of blowing everything  up it also touches on events that  plagued the birds and the landmarks in  the first half of season 4. ruth says in  the trailer my childhood traumas are not  like yours if this is any indication  ruth will likely seek vengeance for  everything that's happened to her  you see  i'm a cursed playing more  it remains to be seen what's in store  for marty and his family but it would be  a miracle if everyone makes it out alive  the reign of the birds and the langmores  is coming to a conclusion with the final  batch of ozark episodes on april 29th  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite tv shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

